note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note run-device-window.om: the Omega successor of tools/run-device-window.sh (Linear DRA-441).
note Build: "$OMC" < tools/run-device-window.om > build/run-device-window && chmod +x build/run-device-window
note usage: build/run-device-window --ledger ID [--dry-run] [--pairs N]
note It runs the same rows as the shell script, in the same order, with the same output lines,
note the same refusals and the same evidence files (rc.txt, window.txt, NN-*.log, NN-*.out/,
note NN-*.out.sha256, cubins/). The shell script's header has the cubin export prerequisite.
note Differences from the shell script, all deliberate and listed in tests/device-window/README.md:
note - the repository root is dirname(dirname(/proc/self/exe)), the physical path of the binary;
note - script_sha256 is the SHA-256 of the running binary (/proc/self/exe);
note - SHA-256 is computed here (FIPS 180-4, adapted from aien-architecture-mv
note   tools/zero-legacy/sha256.om, streamed in 64-byte blocks); no sha256sum is run;
note - NN-*.out.sha256 lists names in bytewise order (the shell used the locale's collation);
note - Omega has no signal handler, so the close of a window opened here is done by a closer
note   process. It is forked before the open, starts its own session and tells this program it
note   is ready (so a Ctrl-C cannot fall between the fork and its setsid). The open's standard
note   output goes to the closer, not to this program: the closer reads it to its end, keeps it,
note   and a child of the closer hands a copy back (so a write to a program that is gone ends
note   that child by SIGPIPE, never the closer). The closer then reads a pipe whose only write
note   end this program holds: on every exit of its own this program writes N there (a window was
note   opened here) or X (none was) and closes it, and the closer runs `spark-window close <id>`
note   at once with the id it kept (the shell's trap EXIT), or exits on X. Every child started
note   after the closer gets, as its standard input, the write end of a second "hold" pipe. When
note   the pipe ends with neither N nor X (this program was killed: SIGTERM, Ctrl-C, kill -9, also
note   during the open), the closer reads the hold pipe to its end, which comes only when every
note   row has exited, and closes the window then: a window is never closed while a row of it
note   still runs on the chip. The shell script closed after the row on SIGTERM and never closed
note   on kill -9 (the lease ran out). A row's standard input is that write-only pipe, not the
note   terminal. On a signal this program dies by that signal (status 128+N in a shell) where the
note   shell script exited 130. If the closer itself is killed from outside, the window stays
note   open until its lease ends, as in the shell after kill -9; this program then says so on
note   stderr and in window.txt, naming the window. The closer is checked just before N is
note   written: a closer that dies in the microseconds between that check and the write still
note   ends this program by SIGPIPE, with the same result (the window is left to its lease);
note - every child (spark-window, git, the torch probe) runs as /usr/bin/env -i -- <environ> CMD..,
note   because execprog starts a program with an empty environment and no PATH search, and
note   execenv is capped at 64 entries and 4096 bytes (the environment on spark-b87b had 78
note   entries and 4796 bytes on 2026-11-16). /usr/bin/env is a host dependency: GNU coreutils
note   9.4 on spark-b87b, sha256 d38fa7db8452a564868961fd5e9a0aa787095676b0fd6e497b766ac40ec65c8b.
note   Its Omega replacement is an execenv whose environment packet is sized from its input, the
note   compiler extension proposed in evidence/device-window/DRA-441/execenv-proposal.md.
note   Environment entries with no '=' or a leading '=' are not passed on (no shell exports them);
note - an argument is read whole up to the kernel's MAX_ARG_STRLEN (131072 bytes with its zero);
note - a command whose output is a value (the window id, a git head) and prints more than 65536
note   bytes is refused, and a window id must be 1..4095 bytes of [A-Za-z0-9._-]; otherwise this
note   program refuses with exit 3 and the closer closes nothing, so that window is left to its
note   lease (the shell would have run `spark-window close ""`);
note - a value or path longer than 4095 bytes is refused (the Linux path limit); the CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES
note   and SPARK_WINDOW refusals of --dry-run quote the value whole, as the shell does. These checks
note   come first, so the order of refusals differs from the shell in two cases, both still refused
note   before anything reaches the GPU: an environment entry over 65535 bytes (exit 3, this
note   program's message, where the shell gives its CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES/SPARK_WINDOW refusal), and
note   a CUDAPP, CUBIN_DIR, CUDAPP_TORCH_LIB or PYTHON over 4095 bytes in --dry-run (exit 2, path
note   limit, where the shell may first give its exit-3 dry-run refusal);
note - before anything is printed or opened, the packets of the open, each row and the close are
note   built once, so an environment that does not fit the packet (65536 bytes and 1024 records,
note   each record at most 65535 bytes: the compiler's execprog packet) is refused at once with
note   exit 3, never in the middle of a window. The git and dry-run python packets are not built
note   then: each holds the same environment and arguments shorter than a row's (the torch row
note   names the checkout path at least twice), so a run that passes preflight fits them too.
text tb "/usr/bin/env\n-i\n--\nspark-window\nrun\nopen\nclose\n--ledger\n--dry-run\n--pairs\nREFUSE: --ledger needs an ID\nREFUSE: --pairs needs a value\nunknown \nREFUSE: no ledger id; usage: run-device-window --ledger ID [--dry-run] [--pairs N]\nREFUSE: ledger id must match [A-Za-z0-9._-]+\nREFUSE: --pairs must be an integer\nREFUSE: --pairs \n < 5\n is out of range\nREFUSE: a value or path is longer than 4095 bytes (the Linux path limit)\nPAIRS=\nCUDAPP=\nCUDAPP_TORCH_LIB=\nCUBIN_DIR=\nPYTHON=\nMAXPY=\nHOME=\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=\nSPARK_WINDOW=\n5\n/proc/self/exe\n/proc/sys/kernel/hostname\n/dev/null\n/../cudapp\n/attach/torch/libcudapp_attach.so\n/evidence/device-window/\n/evidence/device-window\nmaxinterop-device-\n/build/window-cubins\n/matmul-16x16x8.cubin\n/attention-hd128-gqa8.cubin\n/evidence/MAX-INTEROP/68/matmul-16x16x8.cubin\n/conformance/build\npython3\n/build/cubin_probe\n/build/libomega_gpu.a\nomega_matmul_bf16\n16\n8\n--load-only\nomega_gqa_attention_causal\n2\n1\n--expect-reject\n/conformance/run.sh\n/conformance/max_runner.py\n--device\nenv\nPYTHONPATH=\n/attach/torch\n/attach/torch/test_cudapp_torch.py\n/torch-receipt.json\ncubin-matmul\ncubin-gqa-load\ncubin-stale-reject\nconformance-device\npair\n-conformance-device\ntorch-cudapp\nPLAN \n: spark-window run \nREFUSE: dry-run requires CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES set and empty (got '\n')\nunset\nREFUSE: dry-run inside an open SPARK_WINDOW=\nDRY-RUN ledger=\n window=\n pairs=\n out=evidence/device-window/\nWOULD: spark-window open \n --ledger \n --gb10 exclusive --quiet none --lease 20 --wait\nINPUTS\nOK      \nMISSING \n/workspace/maxinterop/venv/bin/python\nrun-device-window: HOME: parameter not set\n-c\nimport importlib.util, sys; sys.exit(importlib.util.find_spec(\"torch\") is None)\nOK      torch importable by PYTHON=\nMISSING torch for PYTHON=\n (set PYTHON to an interpreter with torch)\nEXISTS  \n (device mode refuses to overwrite evidence)\nROWS \n (3 cubin + 1 conformance + \n paired + 1 torch); GPU rows NOT_RUN\nDRY-RUN INCOMPLETE: build missing inputs before the window\nDRY-RUN PASS: plan complete, no device opened\nREFUSE: \n exists; evidence is never overwritten, use a new --ledger id\nREFUSE: cannot create \n/rc.txt\n/window.txt\n--gb10\nexclusive\n--quiet\nnone\n--lease\n20\n--wait\nREFUSE: spark-window open failed; no row ran\nwindow_id \nopened_here \nhost \nstart_utc \nbridge_head \nbridge_dirty \ncudapp_head \nscript_sha256 \ninput_sha256 \npairs \nend_utc \nunknown\ngit\n-C\nrev-parse\nHEAD\nstatus\n--porcelain\n--untracked-files=no\n/cubins\nmatmul-16x16x8.\nattention-hd128-gqa8.\nomega-gpu-\nmax-gpu-\n*\ncp: cannot stat '\n*': No such file or directory\n.out\n.out.sha256\n.log\n rc=\nDEVICE WINDOW \n: all \n rows rc=0\n: FAIL (see \n)\n  \nrun-device-window: cannot open \nrun-device-window: cannot exec /usr/bin/env\ncp: cannot copy \n to \nrm: cannot remove \nmkdir: cannot create directory \nrun-device-window: environment and arguments exceed the execprog packet (65536 bytes, 1024 records)\nrun-device-window: an environment entry is longer than 65535 bytes\nREFUSE: an argument is longer than 131071 bytes (the Linux MAX_ARG_STRLEN)\nREFUSE: cannot read /proc/self/exe\nREFUSE: cannot start the window closer; no window was opened and no row ran\nREFUSE: a command printed more than 65536 bytes where a short value was expected\nREFUSE: spark-window open printed no usable window id (empty, longer than 4095 bytes, or not [A-Za-z0-9._-]+); nothing was closed: check spark-window status\n"
text tcg1 "run-device-window: the window closer is gone; window "
text tcg2 " was not closed here and ends with its lease (see spark-window status)"
